Message-ID: <0736c39292773b7ad08c69773eb5e03039202eb7.1790321839.git.sam@gentoo.org>
In-Reply-To: <eba940f0e0d02a11efaa4a2dc2f20f3c084a322c.1790321839.git.sam@gentoo.org>
References: <eba940f0e0d02a11efaa4a2dc2f20f3c084a322c.1790321839.git.sam@gentoo.org>
From: Sam James <sam@gentoo.org>
Date: Thu, 3 Jul 2025 13:27:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] binutils, gas, ld: Disable SFrames for some tests

These break with a gas configured to emit SFrames by default.

The failures are all harmless, mainly just an unexpected extra section.

For the only non-trivial ones, Indu took a look at some of the PLT tests
where we get a different address for .plt. She found lang_size_sections_1 ()
-> bfd_set_section_vma () just gets called with a different offset which
makes sense given different alignment requirements/sizes.

binutils/
	PR binutils/33317
	PR gas/33126
	* testsuite/binutils-all/x86-64/compressed-1b.d: Pass --gsframe=no.
	* testsuite/binutils-all/x86-64/compressed-1c.d: Ditto.

gas/
	PR binutils/33317
	PR gas/33126
	* testsuite/gas/cfi/cfi.exp: Pass --gsframe=no if supported.
	* testsuite/gas/i386/ehinterp.d: Ditto.
	* testsuite/gas/scfi/x86_64/scfi-x86-64.exp: Ditto.
	* testsuite/gas/scfi/x86_64/scfi-cfi-label-1.d: Pass --gsframe=no.

ld/
	PR binutils/33317
	PR gas/33126
	PR ld/34671
	* testsuite/ld-elf/eh5.d: Pass --gsframe=no.
	* testsuite/ld-sframe/sframe-empty.d: Ditto.
	* testsuite/ld-sframe/no-ld-generated-sframe.d: Ditto.
	* testsuite/ld-s390/sframe-command-line-2.d: Ditto.
	* testsuite/ld-x86-64/sframe-command-line-2.d: Ditto.
	* testsuite/ld-x86-64/x86-64.exp: Pass --gsframe=no if supported.
